# Using Alternate Doclet

To generate output from an alternate doclet, add configuration similar to the following to your POM.

In this example, the doclet is [UMLDoclet](https://github.com/talsma-ict/umldoclet). It runs the Standard Doclet
and adds UML class and package diagrams, as SVG images, to the generated pages.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting> (or <build>)
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-javadoc-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <doclet>nl.talsmasoftware.umldoclet.UMLDoclet</doclet>
          <docletArtifact>
            <groupId>nl.talsmasoftware</groupId>
            <artifactId>umldoclet</artifactId>
            <version>2.2.1</version>
          </docletArtifact>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
      ...
    </plugins>
  </reporting> (or </build>)
  ...
</project>
```

After executing `mvn site`, the class pages in `target/site/apidocs` show the diagrams, and each class and package
has an `.svg` file next to its HTML page.

**Note**:

- [&lt;additionalOptions/&gt;](../javadoc-mojo.html${esc.hash}additionalOptions) parameter could be used to set additional parameters on the command line, specifically for doclet options.
- [&lt;useStandardDocletOptions/&gt;](../javadoc-mojo.html${esc.hash}useStandardDocletOptions) parameter could be used to specify that the given doclet should use the [options provided by the Standard Doclet](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/specs/man/javadoc.html#standard-options-for-the-standard-doclet).
- If you need more artifacts in the docletpath, you could use the [&lt;docletArtifacts/&gt;](../javadoc-mojo.html${esc.hash}docletArtifacts) parameter.
- A doclet must implement the `jdk.javadoc.doclet` API. Doclets written for the old `com.sun.javadoc` API, such as
  UmlGraph 5.x and DocCheck, do not run with current JDKs: that API was removed in JDK 13.

# Using Alternate Doclet In Addition To The Javadoc Doclet

To generate output from an alternate doclet in addition to the normal HTML Javadoc, keep the default configuration
and add an execution of the `javadoc` goal that runs the other doclet and writes to its own
[&lt;outputDirectory/&gt;](../javadoc-mojo.html${esc.hash}outputDirectory):

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-javadoc-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>uml</id>
            <goals>
              <goal>javadoc</goal>
            </goals>
            <phase>package</phase>
            <configuration>
              <doclet>nl.talsmasoftware.umldoclet.UMLDoclet</doclet>
              <docletArtifact>
                <groupId>nl.talsmasoftware</groupId>
                <artifactId>umldoclet</artifactId>
                <version>2.2.1</version>
              </docletArtifact>
              <outputDirectory>${esc.d}{project.build.directory}/uml</outputDirectory>
            </configuration>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
      ...
    </plugins>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

`mvn package javadoc:javadoc` then writes the alternate output to `target/uml/apidocs` and the normal Javadoc to
`target/reports/apidocs`.
